  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/a4g/data-shape#epo-ord-OrderResponseShape">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#NodeShape"/>
    <sh:targetClass rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/a4g/ontology#OrderResponse"/>
    <rdfs:label>Order Response</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>A formal reply from the Seller to the Buyer stating the Seller's ability to fulfil the order. Additional Information: The Order Response is used to inform on the acceptance or rejection of an Order or to make a counter-offer.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment>If contractually agreed, the Seller also may respond to the order, changing details that are acceptable by the Buyer. -- If an order is accepted with change, the buyer and seller need to have an agreement between them regarding the processing of the changed order, i.e. when is a contract concluded and when can the items be shipped. Proposal: If the order response is "Change" then the Buyer will create (instantiate) a new order implementing the changes and superseding the previously sent order.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/a4g/data-shape#ord-shape"/>
    <sh:property rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/a4g/data-shape#epo-ord-OrderResponse-epo-ord-hasResponseDescription"/>
    <sh:property rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/a4g/data-shape#epo-ord-OrderResponse-epo-ord-isSubmittedForOrder"/>
    <sh:property rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/a4g/data-shape#epo-ord-OrderResponse-epo-ord-comprisesOrderResponseLine"/>
    <sh:property rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/a4g/data-shape#epo-ord-OrderResponse-epo-ord-specifiesOrderResponseInformation"/>
  </rdf:Description>
